# GoWalkTheDog — Project Rules for Cursor AI

## What this project is
A Next.js web app for finding dog-friendly parks and green spaces in London. Users browse a map, filter by facilities (fenced, bins, toilets, coffee, parking), get directions, add their own places, favourite them, and log in with email. Live at gowalkthedog.com, deployed on Vercel, backend on Supabase.

## Tech stack
- Framework: Next.js (TypeScript)
- Maps: Mapbox GL JS
- Backend/Auth: Supabase (email auth, PostgreSQL)
- Icons: Phosphor Icons (@phosphor-icons/react)
- Fonts: Fraunces (headings), Outfit (body)
- Hosting: Vercel (auto-deploys from GitHub main branch)
- Styling: Plain CSS in globals.css (no Tailwind utility classes in components)

## Design system — use these exact values
- Primary green: #006947
- Primary dark: #004d33
- Body text: #02301F
- Accent/orange: #DD6616
- Landing background: #9EFF77
- Card background: #FFFFFF
- Icon colour: #209326
- Border colour: #E5E2DD
- Error red: #c53030
- Font headings: var(--font-fraunces) / "Fraunces"
- Font body: var(--font-outfit) / "Outfit"
- Border radius small: 6px, medium: 10px, large: 16px, full: 999px

## Key files — know where things live
- `app/page.tsx` — Main app component (landing page + map view, ~1400 lines)
- `app/globals.css` — ALL styles and design tokens
- `app/layout.tsx` — Root layout (fonts)
- `app/components/MainMap.tsx` — Map with markers and route drawing
- `app/components/MapboxFullMap.tsx` — Expanded map modal
- `app/components/ParkBottomSheet.tsx` — Park detail bottom sheet
- `app/components/AddPlaceDrawer.tsx` — Add new place drawer
- `app/components/EditPlaceDrawer.tsx` — Edit place drawer
- `app/components/AccountSettings.tsx` — Account settings modal
- `app/components/CookieBanner.tsx` — Cookie consent banner
- `app/components/AppFooter.tsx` — Dark green footer
- `lib/places.ts` — Supabase CRUD for places
- `lib/favourites.ts` — Supabase CRUD for favourites
- `lib/notes.ts` — Supabase CRUD for notes (backend ready, UI not built yet)
- `lib/useAuth.ts` — Auth hook
- `lib/supabase.ts` — Supabase client

## What's built and working
- Landing page with green background, dog hero, filter carousel, location search
- Map view with Mapbox, auto-discovered parks + user-added places
- Collapsible filter bar (fenced, unfenced, part-fenced, bins, toilets, coffee, parking)
- Add/edit/delete places (saved to Supabase)
- Favourites (heart icon, saved to Supabase per user)
- Directions (walking/driving/transit, route drawn on map)
- Auth (sign up with first name, log in, email verification, log out)
- Account settings (logout, delete account)
- Cookie banner, footer, legal pages

## Current roadmap — what we're building next
Batch 1 (current): Map pin popup fix, filter bar → white bg, FAB positioning, user avatar in header, favourites toggle, dividers → green, location input icon, map viewport sizing
Batch 2: Account settings via avatar tap, edit details page, forgotten password
Batch 3: Personalised welcome, notes UI, place count, empty states, responsive polish, accessibility
Batch 4: Dog profiles, multiple dogs, photo upload, hero image swap

## Rules for making changes
1. Always tell me which file you're editing before making the change
2. One change at a time unless I say otherwise
3. Explain what the change does in plain English
4. After changes, remind me: Cmd + Shift + R to see it in the browser
5. If a change touches multiple files, list them all upfront
6. Don't refactor or reorganise code unless I specifically ask
7. Don't add new packages/libraries without asking me first
8. Keep styles in globals.css — don't add inline styles unless matching existing patterns
9. Use Phosphor Icons for any new icons (already installed)
10. Use the existing design tokens from globals.css (don't invent new colours or spacing)

## When deploying
- Remind me to commit: git add . && git commit -m "description" && git push
- Vercel auto-deploys from the main branch
- Dev server runs on port 3000 or 3001
